        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(qa): canonicalize scenario coverage metadata",
        "body": "Related: #108429\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a QA architecture problem where live-channel coverage and default scenario membership were duplicated across hard-coded TypeScript tables, `standardId` metadata, and a stale public SDK helper instead of coming from the canonical taxonomy and YAML scenario catalog. Those parallel inventories could drift from executable scenarios, channel eligibility, and emitted evidence.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMakes `taxonomy.yaml` the semantic coverage vocabulary and `qa/scenarios/**/*.yaml` the owner of scenario coverage, ordered execution profiles, channel requirements, and driver eligibility. Runtime selectors now query the catalog; evidence writers read the selected scenario's canonical coverage; channel and driver remain execution/evidence dimensions only. The obsolete live-transport matrix/report path and `openclaw/plugin-sdk/qa-live-transport-scenarios` export are deleted with no alias, shim, fallback, or deprecated compatibility surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo shipped channel behavior changes. QA maintainers now have one authoritative scenario model: coverage comes from taxonomy-backed YAML, a required channel is declared only by `execution.channel`, defaults/profile membership are declared only in YAML, and `qa-evidence.json` records the actual scenario, coverage, channel, driver, and result.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused QA/selector/catalog/coverage proof: 9 files passed, 113 tests passed.\n- Accepted Telegram explicit-selection/control-flow fix: 2 files passed, 104 tests passed.\n- Plugin SDK runtime proof: 1 file passed, 12 tests passed.\n- Plugin SDK surface ratchet proof: 1 file passed, 10 tests passed; public surface is 10,606 exports / 5,341 callables.\n- UX evidence producer proof: `node --import tsx scripts/qa/ux-matrix-evidence-producer.ts --artifact-base .artifacts/qa-e2e/ux-matrix-canonical-coverage --skip-visual-proof`; 3 evidence entries emitted coverage and roles read from the YAML catalog.\n- Linux changed gate: Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxm1ekr64344adfrgfgw6rbx` passed formatting, SDK baseline/export/surface checks, boundary/dependency guards, full typecheck, lint, and import-cycle checks ([run 29458372238](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29458372238), 12m05s).\n- Full build passed on the same Testbox lease (`pnpm build`, 3m24s).\n- `git diff --check` passed. `git diff --numstat HEAD^ HEAD`: 253 files, 618 additions, 1,271 deletions (net -653).\n- Fresh autoreview (`gpt-5.6-sol`, high) reported no accepted/actionable findings after the accepted Telegram fix; patch-correct confidence 0.88.\n- AI-assisted: yes. The agent audited producers/consumers, YAML/taxonomy mappings, evidence fields, package exports, bundled callers, docs, tests, and current-main behavior.\n",
